{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"colossal-slothful-grouse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\n2026-08-12T23:07:07Z rebar-gerrit-voter-errors and 23:07:18Z rebar-review-bot-merge-change-errors both went OK -> ALARM, each on exactly 1 datapoint in the 23:06Z probe minute, and both returned to OK at 23:13Z.\n\nNO voter error and NO merge-change error occurred. Both counts came from a SINGLE journal line at\n2026-08-12T23:02:26Z which is the review-bot's own LLM code-review analysis prose, verbatim\n(CONTAINER_NAME=compose-review-bot-1):\n\n    ...mits matching markers for every target (VOTER_ERROR, MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR, AUTODEPLOY_ERROR,\n    AUTODEPLOY_DEFERRED, gerrit_to_platform error, both interrupt reasons) and REPL_LOG is\n    populated. The rolled-up review_interrupts per_interval=2 arithmetic is consistent\n    (total 14 seeded, next run +2)\n\nThe reviewer was reviewing a change to infra/scripts/observability.sh itself (the cold-start\nseeding fix for widespread-zealous-narwhal / e2a6-9ee4-8d5c-4290), so it enumerated the marker\ntokens as prose. The probe then counted that prose as two errors.\n\n## Mechanism\n\ninfra/scripts/observability.sh section 4 and section 4c count markers with an UNANCHORED grep over\nthe review-bot container's journal:\n\n    vtotal=$(journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=\"$VOTER_CONTAINER\" --no-pager -o cat | grep -cE 'VOTER_ERROR')\n    mtotal=$(journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=\"$VOTER_CONTAINER\" --no-pager -o cat | grep -cE 'MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR')\n\nThe pattern matches the token ANYWHERE in a line. The review-bot writes its LLM output to the same\njournal stream, so any review whose text mentions a marker name is counted as an occurrence of that\nmarker. The probe cannot distinguish its own alarm vocabulary from an actual error.\n\n## Evidence that the counted line is not a real marker\n\nFull-journal counts, real markers are emitted at line start under -o cat:\n\n    VOTER_ERROR        line-start (real): 221    substring-anywhere: 222   offset file: 222\n    MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR line-start (real):   0    substring-anywhere:   1   offset file:   1\n\nSo exactly one of the 222 counted voter errors is the false match, and the merge-change counter has\nNEVER seen a real error in the entire retained journal — its only count in history is this false\npositive, which is what fired its alarm.\n\nReview-bot health across the window contradicts any real failure: voter_voted events at\n23:05:08Z, 23:13:04Z and 23:19:38Z, i.e. the bot was voting normally before, during and after.\nThere is no Gerrit 4xx/5xx, no 409 and no conflict of any kind in the window.\n\n## Classification\n\nFALSE POSITIVE, and the alarm is not at fault: both alarms are correct to fire on a nonzero count.\nThe count was fabricated by the probe. Do not tune the alarms.\n\n## Why this recurs and is getting worse\n\nThe trigger is a review that discusses observability.sh or the marker vocabulary. The fleet is\nactively landing changes to observability.sh right now (the narwhal cold-start fix), so every\nfurther review of that file is likely to re-fire these two alarms. It is self-referential: the\nobservability code's own review trips its own alarms. It also silently corrupts the offset files\n(voter offset is now 222 against 221 real markers), so the counters permanently carry the inflation.\n\nSame false-positive FAMILY as widespread-zealous-narwhal (probe publishes counts for non-events) but\na DISTINCT mechanism: that one is an absent-offset cold start, this one is an over-broad pattern\nmatching the token as data. Both live in infra/scripts/observability.sh.\n\n## Suggested fix direction (not prescriptive)\n\nAnchor the match to the marker's actual emission shape rather than a bare substring. Evidence says\nreal markers begin the message (221/221 line-start under -o cat), so '^VOTER_ERROR' /\n'^MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR' would exclude the prose case. A structural match on the emitted record would\nbe sturdier still. Whatever is chosen must be applied to every marker counter that reads a stream\nthe LLM also writes to, and the same question should be asked of the AUTODEPLOY_* counters, whose\njournal is not currently LLM-written but which share the unanchored shape.\nConsider also whether the inflated offsets should be corrected or simply left to age out.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A journal line containing a marker token as prose (not at the emission position) is NOT counted. Verify: test feeding the verbatim 23:02:26Z line to the voter and merge counters yields 0.\n- [ ] A genuine marker line is still counted. Verify: test with a real-shaped VOTER_ERROR and MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR line yields 1 each.\n- [ ] The tightened pattern is applied to every counter reading an LLM-written stream (sections 4 and 4c at minimum), and the AUTODEPLOY_* counters are audited for the same shape.\n\n## Verification\n\nDiscovered by ops sweep of AWS alarm firings; full evidence trail on childsafe-bizarre-lorikeet\n(b902-18af-14ed-4da1). All investigation read-only (CloudWatch describe/get + SSM read-only\njournalctl); nothing mutated in AWS or on the box.","id":"8c2f-8377-5044-4650","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"observability.sh counts UNANCHORED marker substrings in the review-bot journal, so the bot's own LLM review text naming VOTER_ERROR / MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR fires false alarms"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786576938701881001,"uuid":"d198abc5-ca26-4503-8474-dc1450f2ad7a"}